Paint the nodes after a rebuild so the map is not blank on first load.

rebuildAll() lays out the graph but never calls draw(), and draw() is what
fills the per-node aColor/aSize/aAlpha attributes and the G.vis visibility
flags. Until something else calls it, every node has size 0 and alpha 0 (the
fragment shader discards them) and G.vis is all zeros, so the force simulation
skips every node too. The result is an empty 3D viewport after "Load demo
universe" or after importing an export — the sidebar, clusters and timeline all
populate correctly, so it reads as a rendering failure rather than a missing
repaint.

Mouse movement does not recover it: hit-testing compares against invisible
nodes, so S.hovered never changes and the draw() on hover never fires. Any
control that calls draw() directly (the Labels checkbox, the colour selector,
a search) makes the whole map appear at once, which is the tell.

Verified against upstream 31508ea5630b4404409b468fbab249126ab6c18f: before the
patch a freshly loaded demo universe reports 0 visible nodes and 0 lit pixels;
after it, 150 visible nodes and ~10k lit pixels with no interaction.

diff --git a/index.html b/index.html
index b24eb84..6ead4b0 100644
--- a/index.html
+++ b/index.html
@@ -1803,6 +1803,7 @@ async function rebuildAll(fresh){
   buildStats();
   buildTimeline();
   updateCounts();
+  draw();
   reheat(1);
   if (fresh) setTimeout(fitView, 600);
   toastHide();
